From c050ccccc98c45b792028a320d3e81c189106d22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:09:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Keep agent panel terminal threads in persistent shpool
 sessions

Managed agent-panel terminal threads live in shpool sessions on the
host (local or remote) and survive editor restarts, sleep and SSH
disconnects. Process exit keeps only these threads with a Restart bar.
Remote reconnection retries transient failures with backoff, stops when
a retry cannot succeed and keeps a reconnect action available.

Terminal lifecycle hardening included in this change:
- closing kills the session only after the exact routing succeeds and
  keeps failed closes retryable; unmanaged terminals close without kill
- metadata is retained until the kill succeeds, sanitized (no historical
  passwords) and isolated per row, so a corrupt row cannot block others
- each terminal keeps its original shpool daemon and client locator;
  conflicting clients are rejected and legacy restores stay blocked
- saved terminal roots must exist as directories before a daemon is
  selected; mismatched worktree pairs are not adopted
- shared terminal owners are coordinated across workspaces and windows,
  and a connected owner project is used to close a terminal
- restoration failures are shown in the panel; saved routes are checked
  before the panel restores
- workspace close consent is reversible and keeps the terminal directory
- startup bookkeeping is atomic with insertion and honors configured
  shells; the shpool client's working directory is not reported

